&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of GenAI development, security &amp;amp; governance concepts — a must&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in Data Engineering / Data Platform Engineering / Data Architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level SQL &amp;amp; Python; Snowflake experience required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with DevOps technologies (GitHub Actions, Azure DevOps, Jenkins)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data architecture &amp;amp; data modeling concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building and maintaining replication &amp;amp; data pipelines in a cloud data warehouse or data lake environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with complex stakeholders: dissecting vague asks and defining tangible requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple projects and competing priorities in a high-trust remote environment, wearing multiple hats as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, written, and verbal communication skills, with a passion for continuous learning and teaching, and the ability to produce clear, precise documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will make you stand out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dataiku DSS experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of mentoring or upskilling other engineers on new technologies or platform practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering GenAI architecture guidance directly to business/senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
